<title>PERU: Peru says Q1 sugar cane output rises 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru says Q1 sugar cane output rises 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar cane production rose 1.4 percent in the first quarter to 1.57 million tonnes from 1.55 million tonnes in the same period last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Total sugar imports fell 23.1 percent in the first quarter to $17.01 million from $22.13 million in the same period last year, the ministry added.</p>
<p>According to the ministry's latest figures, sugar cane exports in January and February were up 93.4 percent to $32 million, compared to $16.6 million in the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
